WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:05.560 --> 00:00:16.920
[With These Weapons, Copyright MCMXXXIX, American
Social Hygiene Association]

00:00:17.060 --> 00:00:25.880
[The Story of Syphilis as told by David Ross]

00:00:26.040 --> 00:00:36.140
[Presented by The National Anti-Syphilis Committee
of the American Social Hygiene Association]

00:00:36.320 --> 00:00:41.880
[Produced by Willard Pictures]

00:00:42.080 --> 00:00:46.180
[Direction &amp; Photography ... Russell S. Bushnell,
Script ... Robert T. Furman, Jr., Assistant

00:00:46.400 --> 00:00:51.380
Director ... David H. Lion, Medical Director
... Walter Clarke, M.D., Supervisor ... Edward C. Kienle]

00:00:51.640 --> 00:01:01.620
[Music playing; two scientists are seen working
in a lab]

00:01:01.820 --> 00:01:08.000
In 1905 the scientist, Fritz Schaudinn, made
one of the most important medical discoveries

00:01:08.000 --> 00:01:15.000
of the century. He discovered the spirochaeta
pallida, the germ of syphilis -- syphilis,

00:01:15.320 --> 00:01:18.479
the greatest plague of modern times.

00:01:18.479 --> 00:01:24.490
The positive identification of the syphilis
germ was the first great step toward the conquest

00:01:24.490 --> 00:01:31.490
of this devastating disease. As a mason builds
a house stone-on-stone, so science builds

00:01:31.800 --> 00:01:35.080
knowledge on knowledge, bit by bit.

00:01:35.080 --> 00:01:40.670
Only a year after the discovery of the syphilis
germ, Bordet and Wassermann developed and

00:01:40.670 --> 00:01:46.670
gave the world the first blood test for syphilis.
Syphilis could be diagnosed.

00:01:46.670 --> 00:01:53.670
Then, four years later, in 1910, Paul Ehrlich
in his six hundred and six experiments, produced

00:01:54.580 --> 00:02:01.580
salvarsan, now called arsphenamine. This drug,
when injected into the body, kills the syphilis

00:02:01.590 --> 00:02:02.459
germs.

00:02:02.459 --> 00:02:09.459
Ehrlich's brilliant success [inaudible] Bordet
and Wasserman. Syphilis could be cured. 

00:02:10.800 --> 00:02:15.030
But medical science, never satisfied, marches
on.

00:02:15.030 --> 00:02:22.030
Treatment was further improved. In 1922, Levaditi
found that bismuth aids in the cure of syphilis.

00:02:23.050 --> 00:02:28.810
Hundreds of other scientists added to medical
knowledge until today the diagnosis and treatment

00:02:28.810 --> 00:02:32.790
of syphilis are efficient procedures known
to physicians everywhere.

00:02:32.790 --> 00:02:34.190
[ Music ]

00:02:34.260 --> 00:02:40.940
[Today syphilis can be cured - or arrested
and made non-infectious.]

00:02:41.280 --> 00:02:47.670
In spite of the fact that a cure for syphilis
has been known for 30 years, syphilis today

00:02:47.670 --> 00:02:53.190
is one of the most prevalent of serious diseases,
a leading cause of sickness and death.

00:02:53.420 --> 00:02:57.640
[Chart reading Estimated Prevalence of Leading Diseases
in the United States, Small Pox 5,371, Infantile

00:02:57.800 --> 00:03:00.900
Paralysis 9,511, Typhoid Fever 22,217, Cancer
450,000, Tuberculosis 550,000, Syphilis 6,500,000]

00:03:01.160 --> 00:03:07.080
In America, more than six million people have
syphilis, one in 20. There are a million new

00:03:07.090 --> 00:03:13.959
cases every year. Why? Certainly its terrible
work can be seen everywhere.

00:03:13.959 --> 00:03:20.410
Syphilis strikes infants, kills thousands.
When it does not kill, it may cause blindness,

00:03:20.410 --> 00:03:24.160
deafness, insanity, or deformity.

00:03:24.160 --> 00:03:30.700
In adults, syphilis is a leading cause of
heart disease. It strikes men and women in

00:03:30.700 --> 00:03:37.700
the prime of life, makes many helpless invalids.
Its victims help fill the ever-expanding institutions

00:03:38.080 --> 00:03:40.680
for the insane.

00:03:40.680 --> 00:03:47.680
It breaks up homes, causes many divorces.
Wars, syphilis kills more than wars. 

00:03:48.040 --> 00:03:54.680
Fires, syphilis costs more than fires, floods, or
famine. Why, why when physicians everywhere

00:03:54.690 --> 00:04:01.690
can diagnose and treat syphilis, do we permit
this pale, spiral germ to continue its devastation?

00:04:01.770 --> 00:04:08.170
The answer is ignorance. Ignorance is the
greatest ally of syphilis.

00:04:08.170 --> 00:04:13.630
The rich are penalized by lack of knowledge
as well as the poor. Both suffer because they

00:04:13.630 --> 00:04:20.099
have not learned the simple, hopeful truth
about syphilis, that it can be cured and its

00:04:20.099 --> 00:04:24.060
spread can be prevented.

00:04:24.060 --> 00:04:29.990
Fortunately times are changing. Newspapers
are aiding the campaign against ignorance.

00:04:29.990 --> 00:04:32.669
The radio is presenting the facts to millions.

00:04:32.669 --> 00:04:39.669
Literature is being distributed and read.
Speakers are instructing thousands so that

00:04:40.020 --> 00:04:43.190
they will be able to protect themselves and
others from syphilis.

00:04:43.190 --> 00:04:51.250
[A wide-spread knowledge of the facts of syphilis
is the nation's hope of wiping out this insidious disease.]

00:04:53.530 --> 00:04:59.590
Anyone who thinks he has syphilis should go
at once to a physician because only a physician

00:04:59.590 --> 00:05:06.580
can diagnose syphilis. Early symptoms are
sometimes so slight that they may pass unnoticed.

00:05:06.580 --> 00:05:13.130
The disease develops insidiously. Years sometimes
elapse before it makes itself known. A knowledge

00:05:13.130 --> 00:05:20.510
of the patient's history is the first step
in diagnosis. Then follows a thorough physical examination.

00:05:23.630 --> 00:05:29.479
If sores are found, as is often the case in
early syphilis, a dark field microscope is

00:05:29.479 --> 00:05:36.479
used to determine whether or not [...?]. An
essential part of any examination for syphilis

00:05:36.660 --> 00:05:42.100
is a blood test.

00:05:42.100 --> 00:05:47.250
The doctor takes a sample of the patient's
blood, seals it in a sterile tube and sends

00:05:47.250 --> 00:05:53.680
it to a laboratory. There the delicate and
complicated test is applied. The results are

00:05:53.680 --> 00:05:58.620
checked and then recorded on individual cards.

00:05:58.620 --> 00:06:04.620
Only a physician can interpret the results
of the test. When syphilis is found, treatment

00:06:04.620 --> 00:06:10.889
must begin at once. Early treatment is a patient's
great hope of recovery.

00:06:10.889 --> 00:06:16.960
Cases discovered in the early stages can usually
be made noninfectious and completely cured.

00:06:16.960 --> 00:06:23.960
Even in neglected cases, the disease can often
be arrested and suffering relieved.

00:06:25.150 --> 00:06:31.500
Modern treatment usually consists of injections
of some form of arsphenamine and bismuth which

00:06:31.500 --> 00:06:37.460
can be taken without interfering with a patient's
daily work.

00:06:37.460 --> 00:06:44.270
Treatment must be taken regularly and persistently.
Injections over a period of a year or longer

00:06:44.270 --> 00:06:50.060
may be required for permanent results.

00:06:50.060 --> 00:06:56.070
The patient must also follow the doctor's
orders as to food, proper rest, and particularly

00:06:56.070 --> 00:07:00.580
his precautions for protecting the health
of others.

00:07:00.580 --> 00:07:07.130
For syphilis is a catching disease, especially
in its early stage. Transmitted nearly always

00:07:07.130 --> 00:07:12.960
by close body contact, it spreads from man
to woman, from woman to man, from husband

00:07:12.960 --> 00:07:19.960
to wife and often from mother to unborn child
as it claims its million victims a year.

00:07:20.419 --> 00:07:25.919
Since any syphilis infection is always linked
to one or more others, doctor and patient

00:07:25.919 --> 00:07:32.419
must cooperate to bring under medical care
the person who is spreading infection, for

00:07:32.419 --> 00:07:35.960
treatment makes syphilis noninfectious.

00:07:35.960 --> 00:07:41.039
The treatment of a single case may prevent
the suffering, disability, and perhaps the

00:07:41.039 --> 00:07:44.220
death of no one knows how many others.

00:07:44.220 --> 00:07:44.729
[ Music ]

00:07:44.729 --> 00:07:50.860
[Syphilis can be conquered. Physicians, nurses,
health officers, and citizens working together

00:07:50.860 --> 00:07:54.949
can bring syphilis under control in one generation.]

00:07:54.949 --> 00:07:59.930
With the medical profession as the spearhead
of the attack, the fight against syphilis

00:07:59.930 --> 00:08:05.949
is well begun. Physicians are more alert than
ever to discover and treat infections in all

00:08:05.949 --> 00:08:08.729
persons under their care.

00:08:08.729 --> 00:08:14.240
Free clinics, hospitals, and health departments
provide medical care for those who can afford

00:08:14.240 --> 00:08:18.090
to pay only small fees or nothing at all.

00:08:18.090 --> 00:08:25.090
Health agencies contribute by helping to trace
infections and by teaching syphilis victims

00:08:25.180 --> 00:08:30.220
how to prevent the spread of infections.

00:08:30.220 --> 00:08:35.729
Many states now require that every expectant
mother be examined and her blood tested for

00:08:35.729 --> 00:08:41.829
syphilis, a most important step, for it is
one of the miracles of medicine that modern

00:08:41.829 --> 00:08:48.810
treatment prevents the transmission of syphilis
from mother to unborn child.

00:08:48.810 --> 00:08:53.810
An increasing number of states require that
before marriage both bride and groom have

00:08:53.810 --> 00:08:59.330
an examination, including a blood test for
syphilis, and similar laws are being pushed

00:08:59.330 --> 00:09:04.040
in other states, for government has found
that millions now spent for the support of

00:09:04.040 --> 00:09:08.209
institutions for victims of syphilis can be
saved.

00:09:08.209 --> 00:09:15.209
Industry too is beginning to realize that
war against syphilis is tremendously important.

00:09:16.000 --> 00:09:22.110
Compensation costs, costly accidents, and
labor turnover often chargeable to syphilis

00:09:22.110 --> 00:09:29.110
can be reduced, and so many industries are
encouraging infected employees to secure treatment.

00:09:30.390 --> 00:09:35.959
But the work has only begun. There is much
to do. Government and citizens have a tremendous

00:09:35.959 --> 00:09:42.450
task ahead. Schools have a responsibility
to teach youth the ways of health. For 75

00:09:42.450 --> 00:09:46.580
percent of all syphilis is contracted before
the age of 30.

00:09:46.580 --> 00:09:53.580
Churches can do much by instilling high ideals.
Parents can guide, protect, and instruct growing

00:09:54.300 --> 00:09:59.620
children. Communities can provide facilities
for wholesome play.

00:09:59.620 --> 00:10:05.149
And communities too must enforce laws which
protect you from degrading conditions.

00:10:05.149 --> 00:10:12.149
Yes, there is much to be done, but thanks
to medical science, thanks to research workers,

00:10:12.580 --> 00:10:18.480
physicians, and public health leaders, all
of the weapons for a successful war against

00:10:18.490 --> 00:10:20.820
syphilis are at hand.

00:10:20.820 --> 00:10:27.330
Syphilis can be diagnosed. It can be made
noninfectious. It can be cured. Only one more

00:10:27.330 --> 00:10:34.330
thing is needed to defeat the germs of syphilis:
knowledge of the facts by every man and woman.

00:10:34.480 --> 00:10:41.480
With widespread knowledge and with these weapons,
America can conquer syphilis in one generation.

00:10:43.490 --> 00:10:47.480
[The End]

